Let radeonsi and radv run on kernels older than 6.11.2.

Mesa refuses amdgpu DRM versions before 3.59. Without the check the
drivers run on older kernels, which pkgforge-dev has shipped since
https://github.com/pkgforge-dev/archlinux-pkgs-debloated/pull/65.
A bundle uses this Mesa only where the host has none of its own, so
refusing there leaves the app on llvmpipe instead of the GPU.

Mesa 26.3 raised the minimum from 3.54 because 3.59 clears new VRAM
allocations, and dropped radv's per-application zero-VRAM workarounds
with it. On an older kernel the few games those covered may show stale
contents in fresh allocations. The other checks it removed guard RDNA 4
display DCC, which those kernels cannot drive anyway, and radv's VM
fault report after a GPU hang.

--- a/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
@@ -1503,14 +1503,6 @@
    assert(info->drm_major == AC_AMDGPU_DRM_MAJOR);
    info->is_amdgpu = true;
 
-   if (info->drm_minor < AC_AMDGPU_DRM_MINOR) {
-      fprintf(stderr, "amdgpu: DRM version is %u.%u.%u, but this driver is "
-                      "only compatible with %u.%u.0 (kernel 6.11.2+) or later.\n",
-              info->drm_major, info->drm_minor, info->drm_patchlevel,
-              AC_AMDGPU_DRM_MAJOR, AC_AMDGPU_DRM_MINOR);
-      return false;
-   }
-
    if (ac_drm_device_get_sync_provider(dev)->wait == NULL) {
       fprintf(stderr, "amdgpu: syncobj support is missing but is required.\n");
       return false;
